    "difficultyReason": "Part a is a reciprocal-sum rearrangement: combine 2/h − 1/y into one fraction and invert, similar to p21-q3 f. Part b needs substitution into 2x−h, a common denominator, and cancellation to reach a given result. Part c is a signposted 'hence' that only multiplies through. The algebraic-fraction work is heavier than p21-q3, but the target answers are given and the route is scaffolded. It has no explanatory part or multi-expression proof like p24-q6, so it sits below that.",
